'' T34 (2): a program written with tiko's sized names -- int32, float64, uint8 -- reads them
'' back in diagnostics, where it was told about a 'double ptr' from a 'long ptr'. The names
'' are prelude typedefs, so the unit's own spelling decides (UnitSpellsSized_, unit.bas);
'' type-names-fbc is the same program in fbc's names, which keeps them.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/type-names-sized.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: warning TKO0830: suspicious pointer assignment: a 'float64 ptr' from a 'int32 ptr'
'' EXPECT-OUT: warning TKO0830: suspicious pointer assignment: a 'int32 ptr' from a 'uint8 ptr'
